+// This file covers scope filtering of resources served by aggregated API
+// servers: an APIService opts resources in with the scope.deckhouse.io/resources
+// annotation, and for a scoped read kube-apiserver computes the allowed set of
+// namespaces and sends it to the extension server in trusted headers.
+//
+// Unlike TestScopeFilter, this test runs its own kube-apiserver WITH a fake
+// permission-browser (authorization.deckhouse.io) behind an APIService, so the
+// RBAC floor of a denied caller is computed end to end: the impersonated
+// loopback SelfScopedAccessReview goes through the aggregator to the fake,
+// which answers per X-Remote-User. A second fake, the extension server, records
+// what kube-apiserver forwards to it.
+
+import (
+	"context"
